# `.mutation-audit-inflight.json` was here. The mutation audit's in-flight record
# now lives in the per-user state dir instead ($XDG_STATE_HOME, default
# ~/.local/state): its payload is the pristine text of the file being mutated, and
# this repo's own scanners read that text as findings, so its mere presence in the
# tree failed four tests and gave every mutation a false-failure floor. Ignoring it
# was never enough — the scanners do not consult this file. Not the system temp dir
# either: /tmp is world-writable, and a record anyone can write is an arbitrary file
# write, because the audit hands its contents to writeFileSync to restore from.
# scripts/mutation-audit.ts refuses to run if the record would land inside the
# scanned tree, or in a directory that is not private to the running user.
